= **Movement**

**Suborganizations**

Health of {!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Our party runs and operates a plethora of local newspapers as well as the national newspaper 'Aktuelt'.">our newspapers</span>!}: [+ mediahealth : mediahealth +]

Health of {!<span class="tooltip-text" title="DSU, Danish Socialdemocratic Youth.">our Youth Party</span>!}: 

**Sister Organizations**

Relations with {!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The Danish Union movement is highly centralized under the LO ('LandsOrganisationen', the national organization). The unions are the second pillar of the workers movement (we are the first). ">LO</span>!}: [+ lo_relations : lo_relations +]

Relations with {!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Det Kooperative Fællesforbund (lit. 'The Cooperative Common Union') is a confederation of Danish workers cooperatives, it has traditionally been considered a third pillar of the workers movement.">DKF</span>!}: [+ dkf_relations : dkf_relations +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title=" 'Arbejderbevægelsens Erhvervsråd' (lit. 'The Worker-Movements Economic Council') is a council of academics in service to the workers movement. It was established in 1936 as a joint venture of the DKF and LO. Our party later joined in.">The Council</span>!} owes us: [+ council_favours +] favours




@budget
on-arrival: {!
Q.total_expenses = Q.expense_apparatus + Q.expense_local_chapters + Q.expense_newspaper + Q.expense_dsu;
Q.total_income = Q.dues + Q.income_lo + Q.income_state + Q.income_other;
!}

= **[+ year +] Budget**

{!<table class="budget-table">!}
{!<tr><th colspan="2">!}Income, per month{!</th><th colspan="2">!}Expenses, per month{!</th></tr>!}
{!<tr><td>!}Dues{!</td><td class="num">!}+[+ dues +]{!</td><td>!}Apparatus{!</td><td class="num">!}−[+ expense_apparatus +]{!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td>!}LO{!</td><td class="num">!}+[+ income_lo +]{!</td><td>!}Local chapters{!</td><td class="num">!}−[+ expense_local_chapters +]{!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td>!}State{!</td><td class="num">!}+[+ income_state +]{!</td><td>!}Newspapers{!</td><td class="num">!}−[+ expense_newspaper +]{!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td>!}[? if income_other > 0 : Other ?]{!</td><td class="num">!}[? if income_other > 0 : +[+ income_other +] ?]{!</td><td>!}Youth party{!</td><td class="num">!}−[+ expense_dsu +]{!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr class="total"><td><span class="double-underline">!}Total{!</span></td><td class="num"><span class="double-underline">!}+[+ total_income +]{!</span></td><td><span class="double-underline">!}Total{!</span></td><td class="num"><span class="double-underline">!}−[+ total_expenses +]{!</span></td></tr>!}
{!<tr class="balance"><td colspan="3">!}Monthly balance{!</td><td class="num">!}[? if total_income >= total_expenses : +[+ total_income - total_expenses +] ?][? if total_income < total_expenses : −[+ total_expenses - total_income +] ?]{!</td></tr>!}
{!</table>!}

@politics
on-arrival: {!
Q.members_total_disp = Q.members_total.toFixed(2);
Q.a_memberdecline_disp = -(Q.membermonthly*1000).toFixed(0);
Q.left_strength_disp = Q.left_strength.toFixed(0)
Q.left_worker_strength_disp = Q.left_worker_strength.toFixed(0)
Q.technocrat_strength_disp = Q.technocrat_strength.toFixed(0)
Q.right_worker_strength_disp = Q.right_worker_strength.toFixed(0)
!}

= **The Party**

Current position: [? if spd_toleration : toleration ?][? if a_in_government : in government - ?][? if spd_toleration == 0 and a_in_government == 0 and spd_caretaker == 0 : opposition ?][? if spd_caretaker : caretaker government ?]
[? if in_weimar_coalition and a_in_government: Weimar Coalition ?][? if in_grand_coalition and a_in_government: Grand Coalition ?][? if in_popular_front and a_in_government: Popular Front ?][? if in_left_front and a_in_government: Left Front ?][? if in_spd_majority and a_in_government: SPD majority ?][? if in_minority_government and a_in_government: minority government ?][? if in_emergency_government and a_in_government: emergency government ?]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="A proffesional bureaucracy can help compensate for a weaker membership, however the professionalisation of our bureaucracy also discourages party activity.">Apparatus</span>!}: [+ a_bureau : a_bureau +]

**Membership**

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Our membership count is affected by the internal dissent and long time members dying. /nIt is positively affected by recruitment drives, efficiency and popularity.">Membership count</span>!}: [+ members_total_disp +]0

Last six weeks: [+ a_memberdecline_disp +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The level of activity among our members is negatively affected by the proffesionalization of our bureaucracy and trends downwards over time. \nIt is positively affected by elections, party congresses as well as investment and reliance on from leadership. Our youth movement is especially active. ">Level of activity</span>!}: [+ a_activity : a_activity +]


@factions
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_strength_disp = Q.left_strength.toFixed(0)
Q.left_worker_strength_disp = Q.left_worker_strength.toFixed(0)
Q.technocrat_strength_disp = Q.technocrat_strength.toFixed(0)
Q.right_worker_strength_disp = Q.right_worker_strength.toFixed(0)
!}

= **Internal Factions**

Overall sentiment: [+ dissent_percent : dissent +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The SDS (Social Democratic Society) constitutes our parties most radical left, members of SDS are interested in radical anticapitalist policies both inside and outside our borders.\n\nIdeology: Democratic Socialism, Marxism, Anti-Atlanticism, New-Left, Modernism.">SDS</span>!} strength: [+ left_strength_disp +]%, <br>sentiment: [+ left_dissent : dissent +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The Left-Workerists are made up of our most active union members, they seek to decisively shift the balance of class forces in Denmark.\n\nIdeology: Democratic Socialism, Keynesianism, Reformist Marxism, Trade-Unionism.">Left-Workerists</span>!} strength: [+ left_worker_strength_disp +]%, <br>sentiment: [+ left_worker_dissent : dissent +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The Technocrats are made up of academics and pragmatic modernists, willing to deal with the forces of capital on a case by case basis.\n\nIdeology: Democratic Socialism, Keynesianism, Pragmatism, Modernism.">Technocrats</span>!} strength: [+ technocrat_strength_disp +]%, <br>sentiment: [+ technocrat_dissent : dissent +]

[? if cd_formed = 0 : {!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Right-Workerists are sceptical of the left, the youth movement and modernist culture. They seek to expand the welfare state, strengthen our unions and protect the interests of car and homeowners.\n\nIdeology: Trade-Unionism, Pragmatism, Rindallism, Car Owner Interests, Homeowner Interests."">Right-Workerists</span>!} strength: [+ right_worker_strength_disp +]%, <br>sentiment: [+ right_worker_dissent : dissent +]?]
[? if cd_formed > 0 : {!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Pragmatists are see the left, SDS and some parts of the youth movement as obstacles to our progress. They seek to expand the welfare state, strengthen our unions and protect the interests of the modern worker.\n\nIdeology: Trade-Unionism, Pragmatism, Rindallism, Car Owner Interests, Homeowner Interests."">Pragmatists</span>!} strength: [+ right_worker_strength_disp +]%, <br>sentiment: [+ right_worker_dissent : dissent +]?]


